# Convex Backend Patterns

## Function Types

| Type | Purpose | Can read DB | Can write DB | Can call external APIs |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `query` | Read data (reactive) | Yes | No | No |
| `mutation` | Write data (transactional) | Yes | Yes | No |
| `action` | External API calls | Via `ctx.runQuery`/`ctx.runMutation` | Via `ctx.runMutation` | Yes |
| `internalQuery` | Internal-only reads | Yes | No | No |
| `internalMutation` | Internal-only writes | Yes | Yes | No |
| `internalAction` | Internal-only external calls | Via helpers | Via helpers | Yes |
| `httpAction` | HTTP endpoint handler | Via helpers | Via helpers | Yes |

## Mutation Pattern

```typescript
import { getAuthUserId } from "@convex-dev/auth/server";
import { mutation } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";

export const start = mutation({
  args: { gameId: v.id("games") },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const userId = await getAuthUserId(ctx);
    if (!userId) throw new Error("Not authenticated");

    const game = await ctx.db.get(args.gameId);
    if (!game) throw new Error("Game not found");
    if (game.hostId !== userId) throw new Error("Forbidden");

    await ctx.db.patch(args.gameId, { gameStatus: "playing" });
  },
});
```

## Query Pattern

```typescript
import { getAuthUserId } from "@convex-dev/auth/server";
import { query } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";

export const getByGame = query({
  args: { gameId: v.id("games") },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    return await ctx.db
      .query("gameSessions")
      .withIndex("by_gameId", (q) => q.eq("gameId", args.gameId))
      .unique();
  },
});
```

## Action Pattern (for external APIs like LiveKit)

```typescript
import { internalAction } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";
import { AccessToken } from "livekit-server-sdk";

export const generateToken = internalAction({
  args: { roomId: v.string(), participantId: v.string() },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const at = new AccessToken(
      process.env.LIVEKIT_API_KEY!,
      process.env.LIVEKIT_API_SECRET!,
      { identity: args.participantId }
    );
    at.addGrant({ room: args.roomId, roomJoin: true, canPublish: true, canSubscribe: true });
    return await at.toJwt();
  },
});
```

## Error Handling

### In mutations: throw errors
```typescript
// Convex mutations throw errors (caught by useMutation on frontend)
if (!game) throw new Error("Game not found");
if (game.hostId !== userId) throw new Error("Forbidden");
```

### On frontend: catch errors
```typescript
const startGame = useMutation(api.gameSessions.start);

try {
  await startGame({ gameId });
} catch (error) {
  // error.message contains the thrown message
  toast.error(error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Something went wrong");
}
```

## Transactions

Convex mutations are automatically transactional. If any part fails, the entire mutation rolls back:

```typescript
export const startGame = mutation({
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    // All of these happen atomically
    await ctx.db.patch(args.gameId, { gameStatus: "playing" });
    await ctx.db.insert("gameSessions", { gameId: args.gameId, gamePhase: "game_session_started", ... });
    // If the insert fails, the patch is also rolled back
  },
});
```

## Calling Frontend

```typescript
import { useMutation } from "convex/react";
import { api } from "@/convex/_generated/api";

function StartGameButton({ gameId }) {
  const startGame = useMutation(api.gameSessions.start);

  return (
    <button onClick={() => startGame({ gameId })}>
      Start Game
    </button>
  );
}
```

## File Organization

```
convex/
  tables/               # Table definitions (one file per table)
    index.ts            # Re-exports all tables
    profiles.ts         # profiles table definition
    games.ts            # (future) games table definition
  lib/                  # Shared internal helpers (DB lookups, auth, validation)
    auth.ts             # getAuthenticatedUserId
    profiles.ts         # getNicknameOwner, getProfileByUserId
    players.ts          # (future) getPlayerByGameAndUser, etc.
  auth/                 # Auth domain — exported queries/mutations only
    profiles.ts
    users.ts
  game/                 # Game domain — exported queries/mutations only
    players.ts
    sessions.ts
  schema.ts             # Imports from tables/ and composes the schema
  auth.ts               # Convex Auth config
  auth.config.ts
  http.ts
```

### Rules

- **`convex/tables/`** — one file per table definition, re-exported via `index.ts`. `schema.ts` imports and composes them.
- **`convex/<domain>/`** — only exported Convex functions (`query`, `mutation`, `action`).
- **`convex/lib/`** — only shared internal helpers (plain async functions, not Convex functions).
- Domain files import helpers from `lib/`, never define private helpers inline.
- One file per resource/entity within each domain folder.
- The auto-generated `api` object provides type-safe access: `api.auth.profiles.createProfile`, `api.game.sessions.start`, etc.

## Validators Reference

```typescript
import { v } from "convex/values";

v.string()                    // string
v.number()                    // number
v.boolean()                   // boolean
v.null()                      // null
v.id("games")                 // Id<"games">
v.array(v.number())           // number[]
v.object({ key: v.string() }) // { key: string }
v.optional(v.string())        // string | undefined
v.union(v.literal("a"), v.literal("b"))  // "a" | "b"
v.any()                       // any (use sparingly)
```
